 "caption": "How Como really works. 🌊\n\nBought for about €200K in Serie D (2019). Since then the owners, Indonesia's Hartono family, have put in about €297M, all as new shares, no loans.\n\nWhy buy a broke club? Their streaming service Mola TV wanted a football documentary in Italy, and found Como.\n\nFàbregas joined in 2022 as a player and shareholder, coached the youth team, then led the first team. He couldn't be named head coach without his UEFA badge, so Osian Roberts was, until promotion in 2024.\n\nRevenue: €9.8M in Serie B to €55.4M in Serie A (€31.8M from TV). Tourists: 1.6M a year to 4.8M. Next: a 15,200-seat stadium by 2028.\n\nThe bet: win now, get paid by the brand.\n\nSources: The Esk (company filings), Goal, CBS Sports, Vavel.\nFollow for the business of the game.\n#como #seriea #fabregas #sportsbusiness #soccer",
